  "description": "The scalp: the skin, a dense subcutaneous layer that carries the vessels and nerves, the galea aponeurotica, loose areolar tissue and the pericranium, with the skull usually within about a centimetre of the skin; towards the corners of the forehead the temporalis and its fascia add depth. The supratrochlear and supraorbital nerves and vessels run back from the forehead, the branches of the superficial temporal artery up the sides, and the occipital artery and greater occipital nerve up the back of the head. The chart is an adult's: an open fontanelle (under GV22 in infants) is not modelled. With the patient supine the back of the head rests on the pillow; the model does not restrict access within the scalp.",
